{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791296755565,"sessionID":"ses_eee64f15affexgFGYE8V3pi2KO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1119b54a977bf81b41756","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nfrom ledger.money import format_cents, parse_amount\nfrom ledger.parse import parse_record, parse_ledger\nfrom ledger.report import top_items\nassert format_cents(-5) == '-\\$0.05'\nassert format_cents(0) == '\\$0.00'\nassert parse_amount('0.5') == 50\nassert parse_amount('-12') == -1200\nassert parse_date_ok := parse_record(' 2026-01-02 |  Widget  | 3 | \\$4.50') == {'date': (2026,1,2),'item':'widget','qty':3,'unit_cents':450}\nrecs = parse_ledger('a | x\\n') if False else []\nassert top_items([{'item':'b','qty':1,'unit_cents':100},{'item':'a','qty':1,'unit_cents':100}], 2) == [('a',100),('b',100)]\nprint('edge cases ok')\n\""},"output":"  File \"<string>\", line 9\n    assert parse_date_ok := parse_record(' 2026-01-02 |  Widget  | 3 | $4.50') == {'date': (2026,1,2),'item':'widget','qty':3,'unit_cents':450}\n                         ^\nSyntaxError: invalid syntax\n","metadata":{"output":"  File \"<string>\", line 9\n    assert parse_date_ok := parse_record(' 2026-01-02 |  Widget  | 3 | $4.50') == {'date': (2026,1,2),'item':'widget','qty':3,'unit_cents':450}\n                         ^\nSyntaxError: invalid syntax\n","exit":1,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 -c \"\nfrom ledger.money import format_cents, parse_amount\nfrom ledger.parse import parse_record, parse_ledger\nfrom ledger.report import top_items\nassert format_cents(-5) == '-\\$0.05'\nassert format_cents(0) == '\\$0.00'\nassert parse_amount('0.5') == 50\nassert parse_amount('-12') == -1200\nassert parse_date_ok := parse_record(' 2026-01-02 |  Widget  | 3 | \\$4.50') == {'date': (2026,1,2),'item':'widget','qty':3,'unit_cents':450}\nrecs = parse_ledger('a | x\\n') if False else []\nassert top_items([{'item':'b','qty':1,'unit_cents':100},{'item':'a','qty':1,'unit_cents':100}], 2) == [('a',100),('b',100)]\nprint('edge cases ok')\n\"","time":{"start":1791296755452,"end":1791296755554}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All visible tests pass. Let me double-check hidden-test edge cases against docstrings.\n\n1. `format_cents`: negative values now handled. Check `format_cents(-5)` == \"-$0.05\" ✓. `format_cents(0)` == \"$0.00\" ✓.\n\n2. `parse_amount`: documented formats all pass. But let me consider `lstrip(\"-\")` and `lstrip(\"$\")` — the docstring only documents '-$3.10' style. However, hidden tests may test \"$-3.10\"? Not documented. What about \"-$0.05\" -> fine.\n\n3. `parse_date`: fixed.\n\n4. `parse_record`: docstring example works. Lower-cased and stripped item ✓.\n\n5. `parse_ledger`: blank and '#' lines skipped ✓.\n\n6. `top_items`: descending, ties by name ascending ✓. Check tie behavior: records with equal totals -> item name ascending. With key `(-total, item)` yes.\n\n7. `summary_line` default n=3 ✓.\n\nOne more consideration: `format_cents` with cents between -99 and -1: abs then // gives 0, % gives correct cents. ✓\n\nAlso huge negative: fine.\n\nI'm confident. Let me also quickly sanity check with a small python snippet for edge cases, without creating test files.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1119b54c9001NniTmRaiuluF0M","sessionID":"ses_eee64f15affexgFGYE8V3pi2KO","messageID":"msg_1119b4fa90018FDDBoiL7JABAa"}}
